ing, and releases reserved materials without duplication or deletion. No stock, regrowth, mastery or processing benefit is granted by this review.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Physical effects are finite material separation and effort expenditure, not healing or comfort. Reuse, rather than duplicate, the registered practice:bark-extraction source: only a paid completed practice event meeting its existing qualified milestone test emits practice-confirmed with qualified=true for the performing actor. Temporary feedback is 0.4, capped at 0.5, held for eight rounds, with qualifying repetition refreshing it subject to a 12-round cooldown. Maintained satisfaction uses the same registered source, gain 0.02 and decay 0.001, within its bounded source and global limits; mastery alone does not qualify. A genuinely new finding confirmed by an actual assessment or test may use the existing information-confirmed rule only through its established qualification pathway; repeated facts do not qualify. Requesting, consulting and learning award nothing.\",\"visualReview\":\"Bind presentation to existing declared events bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped. Show assessed eligibility, actual implement reservation, remaining work, separated bark/fines and the changed branch core from persistent state. Replay must show the same paid material transfers and partial results, including cancellation. Keep the source's real geometry and branch-stock display; do not depict bark removal from a standing trunk or display usable bark before it exists.\",\"learning\":2}]}","logprobs":[]}

